# Offline ENERGY_FORCE pin notes — gpw-optb88-forces

## Functional

CP2K 2026.1 libxc-named subsections (`data/xc_section/vdW-DF-optB88.sec`):

```
&XC_FUNCTIONAL
  &GGA_X_OPTB88_VDW
  &END GGA_X_OPTB88_VDW
  &PW92
  &END PW92
&END XC_FUNCTIONAL
&VDW_POTENTIAL
  POTENTIAL_TYPE NON_LOCAL
  &NON_LOCAL
    TYPE DRSLL
    KERNEL_FILE_NAME vdW_kernel_table.dat
  &END NON_LOCAL
&END VDW_POTENTIAL
```

ATV: `XcKind::OptB88VdW` + `vdw_df = true` + `compute_forces` /
`gpw_forces_from_scf` (SC \(V_{\mathrm{nl}}\) in `assemble_gpw_forces`).

## Geometry

Same water dimer as `gpw-optb88-vdw` (12 Å cubic, DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH,
GTH-PBE, CUTOFF 200 Ry / REL_CUTOFF 40 / NGRIDS 4, PERIODIC XYZ).

## Run (offline only)

```bash
source /nobackup/proj/disk/teoroo/personal/jicli594/work/cp2k/install/env.sh
export OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
cd /tmp/atv-gpw-optb88-forces
ln -sf $CP2K_DATA_DIR/{BASIS_MOLOPT,GTH_POTENTIALS,vdW_kernel_table.dat} .
mpirun -np 1 cp2k.psmp -i water_dimer_optb88_vdw_force.inp -o water_dimer_optb88_vdw_force.out
```

Pins filled in `regressions/gpw/gpw-optb88-forces/REFERENCE.md` after the twin run.
